invariant: INV-50
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile puts sha512_compress_blocks.c in sha512_compress.c's
  place in every object that holds sha512.c, a device object among them.
  The file's body sits behind -DCH_CPU_RUNTIME, so a device object
  compiles it to nothing, and its sha512.c, which compiles the second
  arm there, calls a compression function no source in the object
  defines. A linker would refuse the image, but a linker is not the check:
  it names a missing symbol, not the build that lost its source. The lint
  reads the packaged source list per build, and its device row with the
  suites requires sha512_compress.c and bans sha512_compress_blocks.c.

--- old
ifneq ($(CPU_RUNTIME_DEF),)
LIB_SRCS := $(call sha512_host_of,$(LIB_SRCS))
endif
--- new
LIB_SRCS := $(call sha512_host_of,$(LIB_SRCS))
